window.docContents[155].resolve({"/rules/RG1006/#RG1006":{"contents":"\n\nRequirement. Claimed modules declare nothing unsafe or partial; recursion is structural or proved terminating.\n\nProblem. An owned declaration is marked unsafe or partial and is not the exactly authenticated code-generation helper of a safe recursive definition.\n\nAction. Write a safe, terminating definition (structural recursion or termination_by), or move the unsafe/partial code out of the claimed surface.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n","context":"Regula rule reference\u0009Rule index","header":"RG1006: Unsafe and partial declarations require exact helper authentication","id":"/rules/RG1006/#RG1006"},"/rules/RG2005/#RG2005":{"contents":"\n\nRequirement. Owned declarations pass kernel replay from the exact frozen sources; no metaprogram adds unchecked declarations.\n\nProblem. Required evidence is missing, incomplete, unsupported or invalid: owned declarations did not pass kernel admission, a frozen source changed during the audit, or authentication the result needs could not complete. The result is INCOMPLETE.\n\nAction. Remove the construction that bypasses kernel checking (or the source change during the run), then run the project command that collects the missing evidence.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n","context":"Regula rule reference\u0009Rule index","header":"RG2005: Required admission and source evidence must be complete","id":"/rules/RG2005/#RG2005"},"/rules/RG4003/#RG4003":{"contents":"\n\nRequirement. A lean-fail fence fails to elaborate with one error message that matches its whole pattern.\n\nProblem. A fence marked lean-fail did not fail as specified: it elaborated successfully, failed for a different reason, or the worker crashed or timed out.\n\nAction. Make the example fail for exactly the documented reason, adjust the pattern to match one real error message, or remove the marker if the example is valid.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n","context":"Regula rule reference\u0009Rule index","header":"RG4003: Negative examples require completed intended rejection","id":"/rules/RG4003/#RG4003"},"/rules/RG5002/#RG5002":{"contents":"\n\nRequirement. Every public @[regula_material] declaration has a docstring stating its purpose, hypotheses, result and boundary.\n\nProblem. A public declaration registered with @[regula_material] as evidence for a material normative claim has no docstring.\n\nAction. Add a docstring stating the declaration's formal purpose, domain and hypotheses, result and boundary, with a labelled # Intent section (RG5003).\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n","context":"Regula rule reference\u0009Rule index","header":"RG5002: Registered public material declarations require docstrings","id":"/rules/RG5002/#RG5002"}});